{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given two sorted arrays `nums1` and `nums2` of sizes `m` and `n`, return the **median** of all their values together. The overall run time should be **O(log(m + n))**."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/61f113b3-f610-4691-a472-d5f31293bccc.svg",
      "alt": "nums1 is 1, 3, 8, 9 and nums2 is 2, 4, 5, 7, 10: nine values, so the left half holds five. Cutting nums1 after two values and nums2 after three puts 1, 3, 2, 4, 5 on the left and 8, 9, 7, 10 on the right. Every left value is at most every right value — 3 is at most 7 and 5 is at most 8 — so the cut is right, and the median is the largest left value, 5.",
      "width": 854,
      "height": 379,
